<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ket Klao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1545</span> · Also known as Phaya Ket, Ketklao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ket Klao was a king of Lan Na who ruled from 1525 to 1538 and again from 1543. His reigns were marked by factional struggles among the nobility; he was deposed by his son and later restored, then killed in 1545. The Lan Na nobles then offered the throne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/setthathirath">Setthathirath</a> of Lan Xang.</p></div>
